hs support JSON I/O:\n\n```\n>>> \nfrom\n \nase.io.jsonio\n \nimport\n \nread_json\n\n\n>>> \npath\n.\nwrite\n(\n'mybandpath.json'\n)\n\n\n>>> \nread_json\n(\n'mybandpath.json'\n)\n\n\nBandPath(path='GXMGRX,MR', cell=[3x3], special_points={GMRX}, kpts=[40x3])\n```", 'title': 'ase.dft.kpoints.BandPath', 'url': 'https://docs.ase-lib.org/ase/dft/kpoints.html#ase.dft.kpoints.BandPath', 'source': 'ase', 'metadata': {'source': 'ase', 'module': 'ase.dft.kpoints', 'qualified_name': 'ase.dft.kpoints.BandPath', 'kind': 'class', 'name': 'BandPath', 'class': 'BandPath', 'chunk_index': 0, 'num_chunks': 1}, 'score': -3.747921943664551, 'vector_score': 0.5429941415786743, 'bm25_score': 14.383818755224743, 'rerank_score': -3.747921943664551}, {'text': '[ase.Atoms.get_reciprocal_cell]\nmethod ase.Atoms.get_reciprocal_cell\n\nget_reciprocal_cell ( ) #\n\nGet the three reciprocal lattice vectors as a 3x3 ndarray.\n\nNote that the commonly used factor of 2 pi for Fourier\ntransforms is not included here.\n\nDeprecated since version 3.21.0: Please use atoms.cell.reciprocal()', 'title': 'ase.Atoms.get_reciprocal_cell', 'url': 'https://docs.ase-lib.org/ase/atoms.html#ase.Atoms.get_reciprocal_cell', 'source': 'ase', 'metadata': {'source': 'ase', 'module': 'ase.atoms', 'qualified_name': 'ase.Atoms.get_reciprocal_cell', 'kind': 'method', 'name': 'get_reciprocal_cell', 'class': 'Atoms', 'method': 'get_reciprocal_cell', 'chunk_index': 0, 'num_chunks': 1}, 'score': -3.7773380279541016, 'vector_score': None, 'bm25_score': 13.423310210563614, 'rerank_score': -3.7773380279541016}]}

