- get_pseudopotential: Ti and O, norm-conserving, scalar-relativistic (both Z<=54, no SOC needed), pbesol, stringent, UPF into template/. Cutoff hint = 42.0 Ha; converted per INVARIANT 5 to ecutwfc = 2*42 = 84 Ry, ecutrho = 4*84 = 336 Ry (NC ratio).
- setup_jobs.py: for all 51 structures build calculations/NNN/ with copied pseudos (pseudo_dir='./'), pw.in (SCF, MP grid 6x6x8, occupations='fixed', conv_thr=1e-8), bands.in (calculation='bands', nbnd=48 padded, explicit K_POINTS crystal from seekpath symprec=0.01 reprojected onto atoms.cell.reciprocal() with 2*pi factor - INVARIANT 3), bands_post.in (bands.x &BANDS, filband='NNN.bands.dat'), band_labels.dat, submit.sh (SLURM, account m4735, email brent.hu@yale.edu). validate_qe_input passed on 000/pw.in and 000/bands.in.
- run_espresso_workflow on calculations/000 ONLY: success:true, completed_steps [scf, bands_scf, bands_post].
- plot_bands.py: parse 000.bands.dat.gnu (col0 = cumulative k-distance), read n_occ = electrons/2 from pw.out, align to VBM, map band_labels indices to distance-based tick positions (INVARIANT 4 assert that tick range ~= k_col range), merge/split at path discontinuities (Z|X, R|M), y-axis +/-10 eV, saved bands_000.pdf.

ASE FUNCTIONS USED: ase.io.read (CIF read), ase.io.write (CIF write), ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in (pw.in and bands.in), ase.io.espresso.write_fortran_namelist (bands_post.in), Atoms.get_scaled_positions/get_atomic_numbers/cell.reciprocal for k-path. spglib+seekpath for symmetry/primitive/k-path (pymatgen NOT used).

BAND GAP: 1.847 eV (VBM 8.999 eV, CBM 10.846 eV). This is an indirect-ish PBEsol gap; DFT/GGA underestimates the true rutile TiO2 gap (~3.0 eV experimental), which is expected and normal.

